{
	"name": "Ultimate Wrath",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/fire/explosion-mushroom-nuke-orange.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 18th level, your dedication to destroying your enemies and their fortifications has reached its culmination. You may now use a specific form of shaped @UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.class-features.Item.yzRWpRozx01k3Rml]{Splitcast}.</p><p>By expending 3 exertion as part of your casting action you can create up to four shaped areas that deal your full cantrip damage (4d10+spellcasting modifier, 5d10 if you spend an additional exertion). A creature within the area of one or more of these shapes only rolls a single saving throw, but if the creature is within the area of two or more of your shaped splitcasts that require the same saving throw, the save is made with disadvantage. If a target is in the area of two or more shaped splitcasts which require different saving throws, you choose which save they must make.</p><p>You may use this ability once between long rests, freely. If you use it, again, before a long rest you gain a level of Strife.</p>",
